{"type":"message","id":"6f6a59a0","parentId":"dec94d76","timestamp":"2026-04-11T03:18:09.522Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a goldmine! The reservation group has structured messages from what appears to be an automated system (the sender is cli_a935c107cd38dccc, an app). These messages are already structured booking notifications.\n\nBut I notice the human messages (orders from sales team) are mixed in. Let me get more messages to see the actual orders being placed by humans.\n\nActually, looking at this - the messages are already quite structured! They have:\n- 企业/客户名\n- 入住/退房日期\n- 房型\n- 入住人+电话\n- 价格\n- 支付方式\n- 订单号\n- 下单员\n\nThis is already structured data from a PMS (Property Management System) integration. \n\nThe real challenge isn't extracting information from these structured cards - it's that the sales team is communicating in unstructured text like \"改名\" or \"这个取消了\" without referencing the specific order numbers. What I actually need to handle are those plain language requests that lack any structured context. Let me scan through more messages to understand the full scope of what the human sales team is actually sending."},{"type":"text","text":"今天群里有真实预订消息。我看到的是PMS系统推送的结构化订单卡片，这是半自动化状态。\n\n真正的AI提效点在**非结构化的人的消息**——让我往前翻找销售人员的原始文字订单：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_udszfqy06mgi_1","name":"feishu_im_user_get_messages","arguments":{"chat_id":"oc_fe89d2c0436adf59c54747a10131a045","sort_rule":"create_time_desc","page_size":20,"relative_time":"today"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"minimax-token-plan","model":"MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1775877478794,"responseId":"0628f0667c62e08b3b08dd38c8f32f1c"}}
